"""Site-local integrations for this proxy. OPTIONAL.

Copy to `local_hooks.py` (gitignored) on a host that wants proxy events
forwarded somewhere machine-specific — a dashboard, a notifier, a metrics
sink. The proxy imports this module if it exists and calls `on_event` for
each event; anything not handled should simply be ignored.

Keep handlers quick and failure-tolerant. The proxy wraps every call in a
try/except and will log and continue, but a hook that blocks for a long time
still delays the request that triggered it.

Events currently emitted:

    flightaware_usage   fields: count (billable calls used this month),
                        limit (the configured monthly cap)
                        Fired on every reserve and refund, i.e. whenever the
                        running total changes.

Budget thresholds and geo-check enforcement are already written to the system
journal by the proxy itself (via syslog, ident "matrix-portal-proxy"), so a
host whose tooling watches the journal needs no hook at all for those.
"""


def on_event(event, fields):
    if event == "flightaware_usage":
        pct = round(100 * fields["count"] / fields["limit"]) if fields["limit"] else 0
        print(f"[local_hooks] FlightAware budget {pct}% used "
              f"({fields['count']} of {fields['limit']})")
